            <div xml:id="d748">

                <pb facs="0978" n="876" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg876"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/3292: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-12-31T14:00:00+00:00">December 31,
                            1935—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 31—10:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>643. Department’s 401, December 30, 6 p.m.<anchor n="81" xml:id="d748-f1"/>
                    Customs notice number 361 was published and issued by the Commissioners of
                    Customs and Excise on December 23, making arrangement with Yugoslavia effective,
                    beginning December 24, pursuant to Order in Council, copy of which was forwarded
                    to the Department in pouch of December 24th under cover of despatch 1884 of
                    December 24th.<anchor n="81" xml:id="d748-f2"/> No particular reaction given to
                    our communication of December 24 to Foreign Office but it has been acknowledged
                    with statement that subject matter thereof is under consideration. Copy of
                    customs notice just received will be forwarded in next pouch.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
